    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9851" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concĭtātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who excites</i> or <i>rouses, a mover,
				exciter</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">belli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac.
				H. 3, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbae ac tumultūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					25, 4, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concitator et instimulator seditionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Dom. 5, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabernariorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			 § 13; <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multitudo concitata ipsum concitatorem
					antecessit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ira, 3, 2, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
